; ISSUE-043: `(ok)` as a statement (not the tail) of a `!void` function
; reports "unknown: ok — not defined anywhere in this compilation unit",
; though nucleus.error is imported. A clear refusal naming the missing
; result type would also close this; the probe tracks the friendlier outcome.
; fixed-when: compiles
(import-use nucleus.error)
(defn f ():!void (ok) (ok))
(defn main ():i32 (f) 0)
